Provenance of third-party mail inputs

The files under data/mail-public/ come from public upstream test suites.
mail-public/manifest.json records the upstream repository, revision, path,
size, and SHA-256 of each file. Their own terms are under mail-public/notices/.

These inputs come from well-known public email datasets and are reproduced
with their original bytes:

- data/mail-public/sources/mimekit/UnitTests/TestData/mbox/content-length.mbox.txt
  and jwz.mbox.txt, from jstedfast/MimeKit at revision
  0dec05e233a8f018189741d2b682c7b84e5eb4a1. They contain historical public
  mailing-list and newsletter messages from the 1990s.
- data/mail-public/derived-eml/content-length/0005.eml, the fifth message of
  content-length.mbox.txt, also stored for message 83 of jwz.mbox.txt. One
  message contains an old notice that its site content may not be copied
  without permission. The message is reproduced as part of the public test
  mailbox that distributes it.
- data/mail-public/sources/pst-extractor/src/__tests__/testdata/rickroll.jpg
  and mtnman1965@outlook.com.ost, from epfromer/pst-extractor at revision
  7d08ef9bc7112c23275fa948306c76bba6e24fba. The image is a widely published
  music-video frame. The OST contains that image in three attachments.
